<!--
  MANYWATERS_COLOR_SUPPORT_1 v1 — added scope, owner verbatim (paraphrased from
  voice, 2026-09-09): "if the thirst kid is present, we should have different
  bottles of the colored waters too. Conditional mod check."

  IDENTIFIED, live modlist (not guessed): the mod is **Dubs Bad Hygiene**, split
  into `Dubwise.DubsBadHygiene.Lite` (packageId confirmed at
  `.../workshop/content/294100/2570319432/About/About.xml`) + the
  `Dubwise.DubsBadHygiene.Thirst` add-on (packageId confirmed at
  `.../2582878800/About/About.xml`, description "Adds a thirst need to Dubs Bad
  Hygiene Lite") — both active in ModsConfig.xml. The drinkable item itself,
  `DBH_WaterBottle`, is defined IN Lite's own `1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/
  Items_Resource_Stuff.xml:108-167` (ParentName="ResourceBasedMom",
  `modExtensions/WaterExt` with `SeekForThirst=true`) — Thirst has no Defs of its
  own, it only supplies the `Need_Thirst` class Lite's own NeedDef references.

  Each variant below restates DBH_WaterBottle's own fields (the `WaterExt` modExtension,
  `ingestible` block, stack/mass stats) on `ResourceBasedMom` (see FIXED below) and
  differs only in defName/label/description/colour, so these drink and satisfy thirst
  exactly like DBH's bottle — same texture (`DBH/Things/Resource/
  WaterBottles`), tinted via `graphicData.color` the same way the terrain and fleck
  variants are, per this item's colour set (Defs/TerrainDefs/RM_ColoredWater.xml).

  DBH_WATER_MEND_ACID_ON_TAP (C9-F6, 2026-10-15): gated `MayRequireAnyOf` Lite OR full
  `Dubwise.DubsBadHygiene` (workshop 836308268): full DBH's 1.6 defines `ResourceBasedMom`
  (Items_Resource_Stuff.xml:4), the same texture folder and the WaterExt / Graphic_StackCountTech /
  CompContamination classes (strings read from its BadHygiene.dll).

  `MayRequireAnyOf` on each ThingDef (not a PatchOperationFindMod file) — the
  whole node is skipped, never loaded, never a dangling ParentName error, when
  neither DBH is present. Never ungated, per the owner's own instruction.

  🔴 FIXED 2026-09-10 (DIRTY_CODE_REVIEW_STANDING_LOOP_1, live NRE lead from
  Player_log_manywaters_thingclass_NRE_2026-09-09.log — five "Config error in
  RM_WaterBottle_*: has null thingClass" lines, one per variant): the original
  `ParentName="DBH_WaterBottle"` never resolved. Verified against the live donor
  XML (Items_Resource_Stuff.xml:108-109 in Dubs Bad Hygiene Lite): DBH_WaterBottle
  is declared `<ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBasedMom" DBHThirst="true">` with only
  a `<defName>` element — it has no `Name="..."` XML attribute. RimWorld's
  XmlInheritance resolves ParentName only against another def's `Name=` attribute
  (registered in nodesByName), never against defName as a fallback — the same
  engine-verified trap already documented in
  `src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/BiomeDefs/RUT_NightsideIce.xml`. So every
  field below was silently uninherited: null thingClass (hence the config error),
  no WaterExt modExtension (no thirst-seeking behaviour at all), no ingestible
  block, no stats. Fixed by inheriting from `ResourceBasedMom` instead (it DOES
  carry `Name="ResourceBasedMom"`, so that link is real) and restating
  DBH_WaterBottle's own delta on top of it — statBases/comps/thingCategories are
  list fields that APPEND under XmlInheritance, so this reproduces exactly what
  `ParentName="DBH_WaterBottle"` would have produced had it worked.
-->
